  "replacement_goal": "Recognize a bounded reference-free attribute grammar and group IDs without weakening unknown reference coverage.",
  "behavior": [
    "Build one borrowed-module context with an owned group-ID index per GlobalDCE/dependency graph, GlobalOpt or ConstMerge invocation.",
    "Recognize the explicit enum set, bounded alignment and memory effects, plus frame-pointer, target-cpu and target-features strings. Keep all raw records unchanged.",
    "Missing IDs, duplicate IDs, nested groups, unknown strings including probe-stack, and unsupported or malformed forms remain unknown.",
    "Standalone walks remain allocation-free and cannot resolve group IDs without module context.",
    "Recognized groups allow dead-definition deletion, immutable direct-load folding and scalar constant merging; ordinary stores, alias edges and escaped symbol identity remain effective."
  ],
